findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase addressed the from_file_or_default swallowing all errors. The
    config implementation uses from_file with unwrap_or_default pattern. No test distinguishes
    NotFound from parse/permission errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: TEA wrote exit_codes.rs tests covering 'security (error display leakage)'
    and CWE-209. Reviewer verified ServerError Display does not leak response body.
    However, the broader CliError Display leaking OS error details via Io(transparent)
    was not explicitly flagged.
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: TEA wrote siem_client.rs tests for 'header injection prevention' (CWE-113).
    Dev implemented CRLF checks in client.rs:27-39. Reviewer verified. However, the
    deeper issue of using raw String instead of TenantId newtype was only noted as
    LOW by Reviewer.
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: 'Dependencies not declared at workspace\
    \ level as specified \u2014 clap_complete, comfy-table, csv, dirs, reqwest, and\
    \ toml are declared inline in the crate's Cargo.toml, not at workspace level.'"
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Dev implemented #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)] on RawConfig. Reviewer\
    \ verified: 'deny_unknown_fields on RawConfig \u2014 prevents arbitrary fields\
    \ in config TOML'. TEA wrote config_loading tests for token rejection."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: 'config_toml_ignores_token_field does not\
    \ assert error IS raised \u2014 since parsing errors, it silently skips the assertion\
    \ body. The test passes vacuously. It should assert!(config.is_err())'"
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    with 'let _ = config'. The reviewer's vacuous test finding was about a different
    test (config_toml_ignores_token_field), not the default config test with no assertions.
